 "ながめる": "نَظَرَ (To observe or watch.)  [to look at]\nمثال: 何時間も海を眺めた。\n→ I gazed at the sea for hours. / عَجَبَ (To regard with wonder and delight.)  [to admire (e.g. the scenery)] / لَاحَظَ, رَاقَبَ (To take note of and celebrate (a holiday or similar occurrence), to keep; to fol)  [to observe]",
 "ながもち": "دَائِم طَوِيْلًا (Persisting or enduring for a long time.)  [long-lasting]\nمثال: エンジンを空回りさせちゃいかん。長持ちさせたいからね。\n→ Don't race the car. We want to make it go as far as possible. / [nagamochi ; large oblong chest (for clothing, personal effects, etc.)]\nesp. 長持",
 "ながら": "مُدَّة (uncertain duration of time, a period of time) / فَتْرَة (uncertain duration of time, a period of time) / فِي حِين, بَيْنَمَا (During the same time that.)  [while]\nafter the -masu stem of a verb\nمثال: 彼女は身振りを交えながら演説した。\n→ She accompanied her speech with gestures. / مُدَّة (uncertain duration of time, a period of time) / فَتْرَة (uncertain duration of time, a period of time) / فِي حِين, بَيْنَمَا (During the same time that.)  [while]\nمثال: あれほど金を持ちながら彼は幸福でない。\n→ For all his wealth, he is not happy. / كُلّ, جَمِيع (Every individual or anything of the given class, with no exceptions (the noun or) / كُلّ, جَمِيع (Wholly; entirely; completely; totally.) / جَمِيع (Everything that one is capable of.)  [all] / كَـ, مِثْل (To such an extent or degree; to the same extent or degree.) / مِثْل, كَـ (Introducing a basis of comparison, with an object in the objective case.)  [as (e.g. \"as always\", \"as long ago\")]",
 "ながらく": "طَوِيل (Having great duration.)  [long]\nمثال: 長らくお待たせして申し訳ありません。\n→ I'm sorry to have kept you waiting so long.",
 "ながらに": "مُدَّة (uncertain duration of time, a period of time) / فَتْرَة (uncertain duration of time, a period of time) / فِي حِين, بَيْنَمَا (During the same time that.)  [while]\nمثال: 彼は子供ながらにお母さんを助けるために一生懸命働いた。\n→ Child as he was, he worked hard to help his mother.",
 "ながらも": "رَغْم أَنّ (Despite the fact that; although.)  [though]\nمثال: 女ながらも彼女は勇敢だった。\n→ Woman as she was, she was brave. / مُدَّة (uncertain duration of time, a period of time) / فَتْرَة (uncertain duration of time, a period of time) / فِي حِين, بَيْنَمَا (During the same time that.)  [while]",
 "ながれ": "تَدَفُّق (the movement of a fluid) / تَدَفَّقَ, سَالَ (To move as a fluid from one position to another.)  [flow (of a fluid or gas)]\nمثال: 流れは池に注いでいる。\n→ The stream falls into the pond. / تَدَفُّق (the movement of a fluid) / تَدَفَّقَ, سَالَ (To move as a fluid from one position to another.)  [flow (of people, things)]\nمثال: 田中さんの教えるのは歴史の流れに逆らう。\n→ Tanaka's teaching goes against the stream of history. / طَبَق, وَجْبَة (A sequence of events.) / مَسار (A path that something or someone moves along.)  [course (of events)]\nمثال: こういう流れになると結局、どんぐりの背比べになる。\n→ Once things start going this way, in the end they'll all be much of a muchness. / [group of people who remain together after the end of an event]",
 "ながれぼし": "شِهَاب (A meteor, especially a streak of light in the night sky, caused by a meteoroid b)  [shooting star]\nمثال: あ、流れ星だ！\n→ Look! There goes a shooting star. / سَعِيرَا (A fire, especially a fast-burning fire producing a lot of flames and light.)  [blaze (wide white stripe down the face of a horse)]",
 "ながれもの": "غَرِيب, غَرِيبَة (A person whom one does not know; a person who is neither a friend nor an acquain) / أَجْنَبِيّ (An outsider or foreigner.)  [stranger]",
 "ながれる": "جَدْوَل (A small river; a large creek; a body of moving water confined by banks.) / تَيَّار (Any steady flow or succession of material, such as water, air, radio signal or w) / تَدَفّقَ (To flow in a continuous or steady manner, like a liquid.)  [to stream]\nمثال: アルフォンスが空を見上げたまま、速く流れる雲を見つめていた。\n→ Alphonse looked at the racing clouds, his eyes turned to the sky. / [to be washed away ; to be carried]\nمثال: 当時はきれいな水がこの川にも流れていた。\n→ Pure water was washed away to this river as well at that time. / طَفَا, عَامَ (To be supported by a fluid of greater density (than the object).) / طَفَا (To be capable of floating.)  [to float (e.g. clouds)] / مَسَحَ (To clean (a surface) by means of a stroking motion of a broom or brush.)  [to sweep (e.g. rumour, fire)]\nمثال: ジャネットとデイブがあやしいという噂が流れた。\n→ Word got around that Jeanette and Dave were having an affair.",
 "ながわきざし": "[longer type of wakizashi (short sword)] / مُقَامِر (One who plays at a game of chance, who gambles.) / مُغَامِر (One who takes significant risks.)  [gambler]",
 "ながズボン": "بِنْطَال, سِرْوَال (An outer garment that covers the body from the waist downwards, covering each le) / سِرْوَال اَلسُّنَة (An undergarment that covers the genitals and often the buttocks and the neighbou)  [(long) pants (as opposed to shorts)]",
 "ながーい": "طَوِيل (Having great duration.)  [long (distance, length)]\nمثال: 彼に長い手紙を書いた。\n→ I wrote a long letter to him. / طَوِيل (Having great duration.)  [long (time)]\nمثال: 株式市場は長い不振を続けている。\n→ The stock market is in a prolonged slump.",
 "なき": "بُكَاء (Action of the verb to weep.)  [weeping]\nمثال: 見つけた人がもらう人、なくした人は泣きをみる。\n→ Finders keepers, losers weepers.",
 "なきいる": "فجأة بدأ يبكي (To suddenly start crying or sobbing.)  [to burst into tears]",
 "なきがら": "بَاقِي (That which is left; relic; remainder.) / بَقِيَ, مَكَثَ (To continue unchanged in place, form, or condition, or undiminished in quantity;)  [remains]\nمثال: 彼女は父親の亡骸を見て泣いた。\n→ She cried at the sight of her father's dead body.",
 "なきごえ": "بَكَى, عَيَّط (To shed tears; to weep, especially in anger or sadness.) / صَاحَ (To shout, scream, yell.) / بكاء (A shedding of tears; the act of crying.)  [cry (e.g. of a baby)]\nمثال: 病気の子どもの痛ましい泣き声を聞くのは我々には耐えられなかった。\n→ We could not bear to listen to the sick child's pathetic cries. / [tearful voice ; weepy voice]",
 "なきごと": "شِكَايَة, شَكْوَى (A grievance, problem, difficulty, or concern.)  [complaint]\nمثال: 人は泣きつつ生まれ、泣き言を言いつつ暮らし、失望落胆して死ぬ。\n→ We are born crying, spend our lives complaining, and die disappointed.",
 "なきさけぶ": "صرخة (A loud, emphatic, exclamation of extreme emotion, especially horror, fear, excit) / صَرَخَ (to make the sound of a scream)  [to scream]\nمثال: 幼児はしゃべることができないので、ほしいものが手に入るまで泣き叫ぶ。\n→ An infant is not capable of speaking, so it just screams until it gets what it wants.",
 "なきしきる": "بَكَى, عَيَّط (To shed tears; to weep, especially in anger or sadness.) / صَاحَ (To shout, scream, yell.) / بكاء (A shedding of tears; the act of crying.)  [to cry]",
 "なきじゃくる": "شهيق, شهقة (A cry with a short, sudden expulsion of breath.) / شَهِقَ (To weep with convulsive gasps.)  [to sob]\nمثال: 寝室に入るや否や、彼女は泣きじゃくり出した。\n→ On entering the bedroom, she started sobbing.",
 "なきたてる": "عُوَاء (The protracted, mournful cry of a dog, wolf or other canid; also of other animal) / عَوَى (To utter a loud, protracted, mournful sound or cry, as dogs and wolves often do.) / أَنَّ (To utter a sound expressive of pain or distress; to cry aloud and mournfully; to)  [to howl]",
 "なきたま": "رُوح (The soul of a person or other creature.) / رُوَح (A supernatural being, often but not exclusively without physical form; ghost, fa) / كُحُول (A volatile liquid, such as alcohol. The plural form spirits is a generic term fo)  [spirit]",
 "なきだす": "فجأة بدأ يبكي (To suddenly start crying or sobbing.)  [to burst into tears]\nمثال: 彼女は今にも泣き出しそうだった。\n→ She was on the verge of crying.",
 "なきつく": "اِلْتِمَاس, اِسْتِئْنَاف (An application to a superior court or judge for a decision or order by an inferi) / اِسْتَأْنَفَ ((intransitive) to apply to a superior court or judge for a d)  [to appeal]\nمثال: 案の定、あの業者今日になって泣きついてきたよ。\n→ Just like I thought, the contractor came back today, begging for more time.",
 "なきひと": "مَيِّت مَيْت, مُتَوَفًّى (No longer alive; dead.) / مَرْحُوم (Synonym of dead (“those who have died”).)  [the deceased]",
 "なきまね": "دُمُوع اَلتَّمَاسِيح (A display of tears that is forced or false.)  [crocodile tears]",
 "なきものにする": "قَتَلَ, قتل (To put to death; to extinguish the life of.) / قَتْلَة (The act of killing.)  [to kill]",
 "なきわめく": "صَيح, صِيَاح (A loud burst of voice or voices; a violent and sudden outcry, especially that of) / صَرَخَ, صَاحَ (To utter a sudden and loud cry, as in joy, triumph, exultation or anger, or to a)  [to shout (while crying)]\nمثال: 子供はおもちゃの車が欲しいと泣きわめいた。\n→ The child cried for a toy car.",
 "なぎ": "هَادِئ (Peaceful, quiet, especially free from anger and anxiety.) / طَمْأَنَ (To make calm.)  [calm (at sea)]\nمثال: 嵐の後には凪が来る。\n→ After a storm comes a calm.",
 "なぎいかだ": "سَفَنْدَر (Any plant of the genus Ruscus, especially Ruscus aculeatus.)  [butcher's broom (Ruscus aculeatus)]",
 "なぎさ": "شَاطِئ (sandy shore) / سَاحِل (sandy shore)  [beach]\nمثال: 渚に人が群がっていた。\n→ There were flocks of people on the beach.",
 "なぎたおす": "صَرَعَ (To hit or collide with)  [to knock down]\nمثال: あらしでその村はなぎ倒された。\n→ The storm laid the village flat. / غَلَبَ, هَزَمَ (To overcome in battle or contest.) / هَزِيمَة, مَغْلُوبِيَّة (The act or instance of being defeated, of being overcome or vanquished; a loss.)  [to defeat]",
