 "なぎ倒す": "صَرَعَ (To hit or collide with)  [to knock down]\nمثال: あらしでその村はなぎ倒された。\n→ The storm laid the village flat. / غَلَبَ, هَزَمَ (To overcome in battle or contest.) / هَزِيمَة, مَغْلُوبِيَّة (The act or instance of being defeated, of being overcome or vanquished; a loss.)  [to defeat]",
 "なぎ払う": "خَطّ مَائِل (typography: / symbol)  [to slash (horizontally)]",
 "なく": "بَكَى, عَيَّط (To shed tears; to weep, especially in anger or sadness.) / صَاحَ (To shout, scream, yell.) / بكاء (A shedding of tears; the act of crying.)  [to cry]\nمثال: ビルは何時間も泣き続けた。\n→ Bill kept on crying for hours. / تَأَلَّمَ, عَانَى (To undergo hardship.) / عَانَى (To endure, undergo.)  [to suffer (from)]\nusu. as ...に泣く / قَبِلَ (To receive, especially with a consent, with favour, or with approval.) / اِعْتَرَفَ (To admit to a place or a group.) / قَبِلَ (To receive or admit to; to agree to; to assent to; to submit to.)  [to accept (an unreasonable request, loss, etc.)] / تَأَلَّمَ, عَانَى (To undergo hardship.) / عَانَى (To endure, undergo.)  [to suffer (of a reputation)]",
 "なくして": "بِدُونِ, بِلَا (Not having, containing, characteristic of, etc.)  [without]\nمثال: 労なくして益なし。\n→ No pain, no gain.",
 "なくしては": "بِدُونِ, بِلَا (Not having, containing, characteristic of, etc.)  [without]\nمثال: この食べ物は、それなくしては我々の身体が正しく機能しないすべてのミネラルを含んでいます。\n→ This food contains all the minerals without which our bodies would not function.",
 "なくす": "فَقَدَ (To cease to have (something) in one's possession or capability.) / خَسِرَ (To become a defeated competitor in (a game, competition, trial, etc).) / خَسِرَ (To be defeated (in a game, competition, contest, etc.))  [to lose (something)]\nمثال: 彼女は新しい時計をなくした。\n→ She lost her new watch. / تَخَلَّصَ ... مِن (To rid oneself of; to cause oneself to be free of or released from.)  [to get rid of]\nمثال: その国の財政の赤字をなくすには、もっと、たくさんの外国の援助を注ぎ込まなければならなかった。\n→ To get the nation's economy out of the red, more foreign aid had to be pumped in.",
 "なくちゃ": "بِدُونِ, بِلَا (Not having, containing, characteristic of, etc.)  [without] / [have to do]\nafter negative stem of verb\nمثال: 試験勉強をしなくちゃ。\n→ I have to prepare for the test.",
 "なくては": "بِدُونِ, بِلَا (Not having, containing, characteristic of, etc.)  [without] / [have to do]\nafter negative stem of verb\nمثال: 試験勉強をしなくちゃ。\n→ I have to prepare for the test.",
 "なくてもいい": "يَضْطَر (Must; need to; to be urged to; to be required to; indicates obligation.)  [(not) have to]\nafter neg. stem of verb or adjective, expressing absence of obligation or necessity\nمثال: わざわざ彼を訪ねて行かなくてもよい。\n→ Don't bother to call on him. / [need not have ; need not exist]\nمثال: あなたは明日、車がなくてもいいかしら。私、車が必要なの。\n→ Can you do without the car tomorrow? I need it.",
 "なくてもよい": "يَضْطَر (Must; need to; to be urged to; to be required to; indicates obligation.)  [(not) have to]\nafter neg. stem of verb or adjective, expressing absence of obligation or necessity\nمثال: わざわざ彼を訪ねて行かなくてもよい。\n→ Don't bother to call on him. / [need not have ; need not exist]\nمثال: あなたは明日、車がなくてもいいかしら。私、車が必要なの。\n→ Can you do without the car tomorrow? I need it.",
 "なくても良い": "يَضْطَر (Must; need to; to be urged to; to be required to; indicates obligation.)  [(not) have to]\nafter neg. stem of verb or adjective, expressing absence of obligation or necessity\nمثال: わざわざ彼を訪ねて行かなくてもよい。\n→ Don't bother to call on him. / [need not have ; need not exist]\nمثال: あなたは明日、車がなくてもいいかしら。私、車が必要なの。\n→ Can you do without the car tomorrow? I need it.",
 "なくなく": "بُكَاء (Action of the verb to weep.)  [weeping]\nمثال: 先週あたりも誘ってくれていたが、夜が遅いので、泣く泣く断った。\n→ I was invited last week as well, but it was late so I regretfully turned them down. / [reluctantly ; unwillingly]",
 "なくなす": "فَقَدَ (To cease to have (something) in one's possession or capability.) / خَسِرَ (To become a defeated competitor in (a game, competition, trial, etc).) / خَسِرَ (To be defeated (in a game, competition, contest, etc.))  [to lose (a wife, child, etc.)]",
 "なくなる": "مَاتَ (to stop living) / تُوُفِّيَ (to stop living) / زَهْر اَلطَّاوِلَة, زَهْر اَلنَّرْد (An isohedral polyhedron, usually a cube, with numbers or symbols on each side an)  [to die]\nمثال: ディックは１０歳のときなくなりました。\n→ Dick died at ten years of age.",
 "なくはない": "قَلِيلًا (To a small extent or degree.)  [slightly]",
 "なくもがな": "عَدِيمُ الْفَائِدَةِ (Without use or the possibility to be used.)  [useless]",
 "なぐ": "جَزَّ (to cut down)  [to mow]",
 "なぐさみ": "تَسْلِيَة (Entertainment.)  [amusement]",
 "なぐさみはんぶん": "مُتَقَلِّب (Impulsive and unpredictable; determined by chance, impulse, or whim.)  [capricious]",
 "なぐさめ": "رَاحَة (Contentment, ease.) / جابر (A consolation; something relieving suffering or worry.) / وَاسَى, عَزَّى (To relieve the distress or suffering of; to provide comfort to.)  [comfort]\nمثال: こんなことをいっても大した慰めにもなりませんが。\n→ Please accept what little comfort these words can give you.",
 "なぐさめる": "رَاحَة (Contentment, ease.) / جابر (A consolation; something relieving suffering or worry.) / وَاسَى, عَزَّى (To relieve the distress or suffering of; to provide comfort to.)  [to comfort]",
 "なぐりあう": "عَارَكَ, قَاتَلَ (Senses relating to physical conflict:) / تَعَارَكَ, تَقَاتَلَ (Senses relating to physical conflict:) / نَاضَلَ, كَافَحَ (To strive for something; to campaign or contend for success.) / قِتَال (An occasion of fighting.) / مَعْرَكَة (A battle between opposing armies.)  [to fight]",
 "なぐりがき": "خربشة (Careless, hasty writing, doodle or drawing)  [scribble]\nمثال: 彼からは殴り書きの手紙が一通届いただけで、その後音沙汰が無い。\n→ I got a scribbled note from him, but haven't heard from him since.",
 "なぐりこみ": "مُدَاهَمَة (A quick hostile or predatory incursion or invasion in a battle.) / غَارَة, غَزْوَة (An attack or invasion for the purpose of making arrests, seizing property, or pl) / أَغَارَ, اِقْتَحَمَ (To engage in a raid against.) / أَغَارَ (To indulge oneself by taking from.)  [raid]",
 "なぐりこむ": "مُدَاهَمَة (A quick hostile or predatory incursion or invasion in a battle.) / غَارَة, غَزْوَة (An attack or invasion for the purpose of making arrests, seizing property, or pl) / أَغَارَ, اِقْتَحَمَ (To engage in a raid against.) / أَغَارَ (To indulge oneself by taking from.)  [to raid]",
 "なぐりたおす": "صَرَعَ (To hit or collide with)  [to knock down]\nمثال: 他人をなぐり倒す権利がないのと同様に、無礼な言葉を浴びせる権利もない。\n→ We have no more right to say a rude thing to another than to knock him down.",
 "なぐり倒す": "صَرَعَ (To hit or collide with)  [to knock down]\nمثال: 他人をなぐり倒す権利がないのと同様に、無礼な言葉を浴びせる権利もない。\n→ We have no more right to say a rude thing to another than to knock him down.",
 "なぐる": "ضَرَبَ (To have a sharp or sudden physical effect, as of a blow.) / إِضْرَاب (A work stoppage (or otherwise concerted stoppage of an activity) as a form of pr)  [to strike]\nمثال: ジョージは彼の腹を殴った。\n→ George hit him in the stomach.",
 "なけなし": "بَخْس (meager; worthless; pitiful; trifling)  [paltry]\nمثال: なけなしの金を取っていった。\n→ He took away what little money I had.",
