 "なんてったって": "مَهْمَا (Regardless of, in spite of, whatever.)  [no matter what]",
 "なんてん": "خَطَأ (Culpability; the responsibility for a blameworthy event.) / صَدْع, فَالِق (A point at which something is divided, interrupted, or disconnected.)  [fault]\nمثال: あそこの食べ物はうまいし値段も安いが、地の利が悪いのが難点だね。\n→ That place's food is great, and their prices are good, but the fly in the ointment is their terrible location. / مَرْبِط الْفَرَس (The basic, central, or essential point or feature.)  [crux (of a matter)]\nمثال: ただし押し込む瞬間気圧の変化のせいでしょうか、耳がツンとするのが難点です。\n→ However, maybe from the sudden change in pressure when you push them in, having your ears pop is a problem.",
 "なんで": "لِأَنَّ (By or for the cause that; on this account that; for the reason that.) / هكذا, بلا سبب (Used alone to refuse to provide a full answer to a question begun with \"why\", us)  [because]\nafter nouns or na-adjectives\nمثال: 慌て者なので彼はきっと早とちりをするだろう。\n→ Being a hasty person, he is likely to jump to conclusions. / إِذَنْ, لِذٰلِكَ (Consequently, by or in consequence of that or this cause; referring to something)  [therefore]\nat sentence beginning",
 "なんであれ": "أَيّ, أَيَّمَا (Regardless of the ... that; for any ... that.) / مَهْمَا مَا (What ever; emphasised form of 'what', used to ask which thing, event, circumstan) / طُز (A holophrastic expression used to dismiss something that the speaker doesn't car)  [whatever]\nمثال: なんであれ物事の本体を捕らえる事が肝心だ。\n→ No matter what the problem is, it's essential to get at the heart of the matter.",
 "なんでい": "حَمَأ, حَمأَة (A residual semi-solid material left from industrial, water treatment, or wastewa) / رُسَابَة (A sediment of accumulated minerals in a steam boiler.)  [sludge]",
 "なんでかというと": "لِأَنَّ (By or for the cause that; on this account that; for the reason that.) / هكذا, بلا سبب (Used alone to refuse to provide a full answer to a question begun with \"why\", us)  [because]",
 "なんでも": "أَيّ (One at all; at least one; at least one kind of; some; a positive quantity of.) / أَيّ (A/an, each or some, no matter its/their identity or nature.) / أَيّ, كُلّ (Any thing(s) or person(s).)  [any]\nمثال: この犬は何でもほとんど食べます。\n→ This dog eats almost anything. / [I am told ; I hear]\nat start of sentence",
 "なんでもかでも": "كُلّ شَيْء (All the things under discussion.)  [(anything and) everything] / [by all means ; at any cost]",
 "なんでもかんでも": "كُلّ شَيْء (All the things under discussion.)  [(anything and) everything]\nمثال: 聞いた事をなんでもかんでも信じてはいけない。\n→ Don't believe everything you hear. / [by all means ; at any cost]",
 "なんでもない": "سَهْل (Requiring little skill or effort.)  [easy]\nمثال: 何でもないことに大騒ぎするのはやめなさい。\n→ Stop making a fuss over nothing. / عَفْوًا, عَلَى الرُحْب وَالسَّعَة (A conventional reply to an expression of gratitude.)  [not at all]\nin the form of 〜でもなんでもない",
 "なんと": "يَا لَ (Emphasises that something is noteworthy or remarkable in quality or degree, in e) / مَا (That which; those that; the thing(s) that.) / مَاذَا, مَا (Anything that; all that; whatever.)  [what]\nمثال: 英語でこの昆虫を何といいますか。\n→ What do you call this insect in English? / [what (a) ...! ; how ...!]\nindicates surprise, admiration, etc.\nمثال: なんと素晴らしい発明だろう。\n→ What a wonderful invention! / صدق أو لا تصدق (This may be surprising, but it's true.)  [believe it or not] / عَجَبًا (An indication of excitement, surprise, astonishment, or pleasure.) / سُبْحَانَ الله (An expression of amazement, awe, or admiration.)  [wow]",
 "なんという": "كَيْف, ازاي (In what manner) / كَيْفَ, ازاي (In what manner:) / كَيْفَ, ازاي (In what state or condition.) / كَمْ, يَا لَ (Used as a modifier to indicate surprise, delight, or other strong feelings in an)  [how (beautiful, tasty, etc.)]\nمثال: なんというばかげた考えだ。\n→ What an absurd idea! / [nothing worth mentioning ; nothing special]\nwith neg. verb, esp. as ～こともない / [of what name]",
 "なんというか": "حَبَّ (to enjoy) / أَحَبَّ (to enjoy) / اِسْتَمْطَعَ (to enjoy) / أَعْجَبَ (to enjoy) / مِثْل (Similar.) / مِثْل, شِبْه (Someone similar to a given person, or something similar to a given object; a com) / مِثْل, كَـ (Similar to, reminiscent of.) / مِثْل, كَـ (Such as; including.)  [like]",
 "なんといったって": "مَهْمَا (Regardless of, in spite of, whatever.)  [no matter what]",
 "なんとか": "شَيْء (An uncertain or unspecified thing; one thing.)  [something] / بِطَرِيقَةٍ أَو بِأُخرَى (By any means possible.)  [one way or another]\nمثال: なんとかその機械を動かした。\n→ He managed to run the machine.",
 "なんとかして": "بِطَرِيقَةٍ أَو بِأُخرَى (By any means possible.)  [one way or another]",
 "なんとしてでも": "بِأَيِّ ثَمَنٍ (As an absolute imperative; sparing no effort or expense)  [at all costs]\nمثال: 私は何としてでも自分の目的を成し遂げます。\n→ I will accomplish my purpose at any cost.",
 "なんとしても": "بِأَيِّ ثَمَنٍ (As an absolute imperative; sparing no effort or expense)  [at all costs]\nمثال: 医者と看護婦はなんとしても生命を守らなければならない。\n→ Doctors and nurses must preserve life at all costs.",
 "なんとでも": "أَيّ, أَيَّمَا (Regardless of the ... that; for any ... that.) / مَهْمَا مَا (What ever; emphasised form of 'what', used to ask which thing, event, circumstan) / طُز (A holophrastic expression used to dismiss something that the speaker doesn't car)  [whatever]",
 "なんとなれば": "لِأَنَّ (By or for the cause that; on this account that; for the reason that.) / هكذا, بلا سبب (Used alone to refuse to provide a full answer to a question begun with \"why\", us)  [because]",
 "なんとも": "حَقًّا (Actually; in fact; in reality.) / وَٱللّٰه؟ (indicating surprise at, or requesting confirmation of, some ) / لَيْسَ مَعْقُل! (indicating surprise at, or requesting confirmation of, some ) / حَقًّا (indicating surprise at, or requesting confirmation of, some )  [really]\nمثال: 何とも言いようがないなあ。\n→ I just don't know what to say. / أَيُّ شَيْءٍ (Any object, act, state, event, or fact whatsoever; a thing of any kind; somethin)  [(not) anything]\nwith neg. verb",
 "なんともない": "أَمِين, سَالِم (Not in danger; out of harm's reach.) / خَزْنَة حَدِيدِيَّة, خَزْنَة (A box, usually made of metal, in which valuables can be locked for safekeeping.)  [safe (and sound)]",
 "なんともはや": "حَقًّا (Actually; in fact; in reality.) / وَٱللّٰه؟ (indicating surprise at, or requesting confirmation of, some ) / لَيْسَ مَعْقُل! (indicating surprise at, or requesting confirmation of, some ) / حَقًّا (indicating surprise at, or requesting confirmation of, some )  [really]\nemphatic",
 "なんとゆう": "كَيْف, ازاي (In what manner) / كَيْفَ, ازاي (In what manner:) / كَيْفَ, ازاي (In what state or condition.) / كَمْ, يَا لَ (Used as a modifier to indicate surprise, delight, or other strong feelings in an)  [how (beautiful, tasty, etc.)]\nمثال: なんというばかげた考えだ。\n→ What an absurd idea! / [nothing worth mentioning ; nothing special]\nwith neg. verb, esp. as ～こともない / [of what name]",
 "なんと言うか": "حَبَّ (to enjoy) / أَحَبَّ (to enjoy) / اِسْتَمْطَعَ (to enjoy) / أَعْجَبَ (to enjoy) / مِثْل (Similar.) / مِثْل, شِبْه (Someone similar to a given person, or something similar to a given object; a com) / مِثْل, كَـ (Similar to, reminiscent of.) / مِثْل, كَـ (Such as; including.)  [like]",
 "なんど": "عَرِين, حُجْرَة (Any private or inner room, (particularly):) / خِزَانَة (A private cabinet, (particularly):)  [closet] / [grayish blue]",
 "なんどき": "مَتَى (at what time, as a direct question) / إمتى (at what time, as a direct question) / متى (at what time, as a direct question) / متى (at what time, as a direct question) / امتى (at what time, as a direct question) / فوقتاش (at what time, as a direct question) / حِينَمَا, عِنْدَمَا (During the time that; at the time of the action of the following clause or parti) / مَتَى (At what time; at which time.)  [when]\nusu. as いつ何時 / [what time]",
 "なんどきでも": "دَائِمًا, أَبَدًا (At all times; throughout all time; since the beginning.)  [always]\nمثال: 私はいつでも喜んでお手伝いします。\n→ I am always ready to help you. / مَتَى, مَتَى مَا (At any time that.) / كُلَّمَا (Every time that.)  [whenever (you like)]\nمثال: あなたはいつでも歓迎されています。\n→ You will be welcome at any time.",
 "なんどくか": "تَعْتِيم (The act or process of obfuscating, or obscuring the perception of something; the)  [obfuscation (of source code)]",
 "なんどとなく": "طورا بعد طور (Again and again; repeatedly; every time; always; time and again.)  [time after time]",
 "なんども": "كَثِيرًا, غَالِبًا (Frequently; many times on different occasions.)  [often]\nمثال: 彼は戦場で何度も死をうまく逃れた。\n→ He cheated death many times on the battlefield.",
 "なんなく": "بِسُهُولَة (Without difficulty.)  [easily]\nمثال: 彼はその手品を難無くやって見せた。\n→ He performed the trick with ease.",
 "なんなら": "[if you like ; if you prefer]\nمثال: 何ならジョージの職場に電話をして、すぐ帰宅してお前を手伝うようにと伝えようかい。\n→ In fact, I'll even call George at the office and tell him he ought to come home and help out. / [if ... doesn't suit you ; if you don't like ...]\nas ...が何なら / عِلَاوَة عَلَى ذٰلِكَ, أَضِف إِلَى ذٰلِك (In addition; besides; further; what's more (i.e. to denote additional informatio)  [furthermore] / آنَذَاكَ, حِينَئِذٍ (At that time.) / ثُمَّ (Soon afterward.) / ثُمَّ (Next in order of place.) / إِذًا, إِذَنْ (In that case.)  [then]",
 "なんなり": "أَيُّ شَيْءٍ (Any object, act, state, event, or fact whatsoever; a thing of any kind; somethin)  [anything]\nمثال: 何なりと言って下さい。\n→ Just tell me what you'd like me to do.",
 "なんなりと": "أَيُّ شَيْءٍ (Any object, act, state, event, or fact whatsoever; a thing of any kind; somethin)  [anything]",
 "なんなりとも": "أَيُّ شَيْءٍ (Any object, act, state, event, or fact whatsoever; a thing of any kind; somethin)  [anything]",
 "なんなんとす": "اِقْتَرَبَ (To come or go near, in place or time; to move toward; to advance nearer; to draw) / اِقْتِرَاب, مُقَارَبَة (An act of drawing near in place or time; an advancing or coming near.) / كَيْفِيَّة, طَرِيقَة (A manner of making (a policy) or solving (a problem, etc.).)  [to approach]",
 "なんなんとする": "اِقْتَرَبَ (To come or go near, in place or time; to move toward; to advance nearer; to draw) / اِقْتِرَاب, مُقَارَبَة (An act of drawing near in place or time; an advancing or coming near.) / كَيْفِيَّة, طَرِيقَة (A manner of making (a policy) or solving (a problem, etc.).)  [to approach]",
 "なんにしろ": "عَلَى كُلِّ حَال, على كل حال (Regardless; anyhow.) / عَلَى أَيُّ حَالٍ, على كل حال (Used to indicate that a statement explains or supports a previous statement. See)  [anyway]",
 "なんにせよ": "عَلَى كُلِّ حَال, على كل حال (Regardless; anyhow.) / عَلَى أَيُّ حَالٍ, على كل حال (Used to indicate that a statement explains or supports a previous statement. See)  [anyway]",
 "なんにでも": "كُلّ شَيْء (All the things under discussion.)  [everything]\nمثال: 要するに彼は何にでも飽きるのだ。\n→ In a word, he tires of everything.",
 "なんにも": "أَيُّ شَيْءٍ (Any object, act, state, event, or fact whatsoever; a thing of any kind; somethin)  [(not) anything]\nwith neg. verb\nمثال: このロボット何でも私の言うことを聞くんだ。疲れて、何にもしたくない時は、助かるね。なんて、ありえない話だよね。\n→ This robot does whatever I say. That's a big help when I'm too tired to do anything. Not too likely, huh?",
 "なんにもならない": "عَقِيم (Unproductive, useless.)  [fruitless]\nمثال: 彼の過去の成功は何にもならない。\n→ His past successes count for nothing.",
 "なんねい": "نَانِّينْغ, ناننينغ (A prefecture-level city, the capital of the Guangxi autonomous region, China.)  [Nanning (China)]",
 "なんねん": "كَم وَقْتًا, إِلَى مَتَى (Used literally: for what duration.)  [how long]\nمثال: それを建てるのに何年もかかった。\n→ It took many years to build it. / [what year]",
 "なんの": "يَا لَ (Emphasises that something is noteworthy or remarkable in quality or degree, in e) / مَا (That which; those that; the thing(s) that.) / مَاذَا, مَا (Anything that; all that; whatever.)  [what]\nمثال: 何の目的で彼はここに来たのか。\n→ For what purpose did he come here? / أَيّ (One at all; at least one; at least one kind of; some; a positive quantity of.) / أَيّ (A/an, each or some, no matter its/their identity or nature.) / أَيّ, كُلّ (Any thing(s) or person(s).)  [any]\nwith. neg. sentence\nمثال: その噂はなんの根拠もなかった。\n→ The rumor was without foundation. / [adds emphasis to the preceding word]\nas ...のなんの\nمثال: 彼女、美しいのなんのって・・・！\n→ She is beautiful and how! / لَا (Not any.) / نَعَم (Used to show agreement with a negative question.) / لَا, لَاءَان (A negating expression; an answer that shows disagreement, denial, refusal, or di) / لَا (A vote not in favor, or opposing a proposition.)  [no]\nused to dismiss someone's concerns, words, etc.",
 "なんのきなしに": "عَنْ غَفْلَةٍ (Without meaning to, in an unintentional manner, not intentionally.)  [unintentionally]\nمثال: なんの気なしに言っただけで、別に悪気があってのことではありません。\n→ I just said so without thinking much about it. I didn't mean anything serious.",
