 "はめる": "لَاقَ (To be suitable for.) / نَاسَبَ, لَاقَ (To conform to in size and shape.) / نَاسَبَ (To be of the right size and shape)  [to fit (e.g. a pane into a frame)]\nمثال: 彼の肖像画は装飾の施された額縁にはめられた。\n→ His portrait was mounted in the fancy frame. / لَبِسَ, اِرْتَدَى (To don (clothing, equipment, or the like).)  [to put on (something that envelops; e.g. a ring, gloves)]\nمثال: 彼女は左手の薬指にダイヤの指輪をはめていた。\n→ She wore a diamond ring on her left third finger. / قُوَّة (Ability to influence; strength or energy of body or mind; active power; vigour; ) / قُوَّة (Anything that is able to make a substantial change in a person or thing.) / أَجْبَرَ, اِضْطَرَّ (To compel (an adversary or partner) to trump a trick by leading a suit that he/s)  [to force (into a mold)] / خَدَعَ, غَشَّ (To trick or mislead.)  [to deceive]\nمثال: 奴が俺をわなにはめてスキャンダルにおとしいれた。\n→ He set me up for the scandal.",
