 "はやく": "بَاكِر (At a time in advance of the usual or expected event.) / مُبَكِّرًا, بَاكِرًا (At a time before expected; sooner than usual.)  [early]\nمثال: それが君の生活をよくするのに役立つなら、いくら早くとりかかっても早すぎることはないよ。\n→ If it is useful for improving your life, it cannot be done too soon. / بِسُرْعَة, عَاجِلًا (Rapidly; with speed; fast; with expedition.)  [quickly]\nesp. 速く\nمثال: あなたが早くよくなるように祈っています。\n→ We are hoping for your quick recovery.",
 "はやくも": "قَد, مِنْ قَبْلُ (Prior to some specified time, either past, present, or future; by this time; pre) / لقد (So soon.)  [already]\nمثال: まずいよ。また遅刻だ！！はやくも遅刻魔の異名をとってしまう。\n→ Oh no! I'm late again!! I'm going to get the nickname 'King of Late arrival'. / [at the earliest ; at the soonest]",
 "はやさ": "سُرْعَة (The state of moving quickly or the capacity for rapid motion.) / سُرْعَة (The rate of motion or action, specifically the magnitude of the velocity; the ra)  [speed]\nesp. 速さ\nمثال: エイズウイルスの拡散は恐るべき速さで進んでいる。\n→ The speed of the spread of AIDS is horrifyingly fast. / [earliness]\nesp. 早さ",
 "はやし": "خَشَب, خشب (The substance making up the central part of the trunk and branches of a tree. Us)  [wood]\nمثال: 林に竹が目立つ。\n→ Bamboo stands out in the woods. / حُزْمَة, عُنْقُود (A group of similar things, either growing together, or in a cluster or clump, us) / مَجْمُوعَة (An informal body of friends.) / حُزْمَة (A considerable amount.) / حَزَمَ (To gather into a bunch.)  [bunch (of something)]",
